n" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406986 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186407001 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406986 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046665 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406986 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048498 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406986 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "13211b98-9cdf-5456-a254-0f2d03a88cbb" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406987 #edb/ref 1081 "A triangle" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406987 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406987 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "0fc064fc-557b-51b4-acc4-5e5aac84e9ea" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406988 #edb/ref 1081 "A line segment" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406988 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406988 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "394dd73f-cf48-54c7-81fb-4dd53a787045" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406989 #edb/ref 1081 "-3" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406989 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406989 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "3f998697-e815-585e-b0b5-3820b9ab9a03" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406990 #edb/ref 1081 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406990 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406990 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "51054506-a98c-59d1-82db-eab8461f2cb2" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406991 #edb/ref 1081 "13" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406991 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406991 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "6c76efec-c230-59b8-bab5-b44500517e1e" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406992 #edb/ref 1081 "A square" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406992 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406992 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "72653cf4-8cbf-523e-b1d8-e878cfd112ab" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406993 #edb/ref 1081 "9" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406993 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406993 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "80f4eee2-e47a-55c2-b5f0-e42eb70ff849" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406994 #edb/ref 1081 "7" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406994 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406994 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "c3375fbb-f890-5cba-a4b4-7f53a73a78cb" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406995 #edb/ref 1081 "A pentagon" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406995 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406995 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "c61e03b3-7008-5b09-9b8a-dd9dc056f91b" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406996 #edb/ref 1081 "A point" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406996 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406996 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "d1b9f565-9eda-5c15-bc7f-e57e8c6bdef5" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406997 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406989 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406997 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406990 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406997 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406991 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406997 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406993 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406997 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406994 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406997 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406997 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406997 #edb/ref 1079 #edb/ref 17592186406991 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406997 #edb/ref 1080 #uuid "20065c9e-4427-527a-a708-a46b3d2f2065" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406998 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406987 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406998 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406988 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406998 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406992 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406998 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406995 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406998 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406996 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406998 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406998 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406998 #edb/ref 1079 #edb/ref 17592186406988 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406998 #edb/ref 1080 #uuid "2eef93f6-f290-530b-8af5-dd127f8894d8" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406999 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186406998 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406999 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162221" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406999 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406999 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/99/99b3d68b7f0c89ba430b098f9e7fda95f3013f310060dd71cf86eacc6e51afa7.png)\n\nConsider the affine transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \nWhat would be the image of the quadrilateral shown above under the action of $T?$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406999 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "353e50fd-8521-51a5-ae98-273dc887e6d8" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186406999 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that for any affine transformation \n\n$$\nT:u⟶Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $u$ and $b$ are $2\\times 1$ column vectors, we have one of the following three possibilities:\n\n- If $T$ is non-singular, i.e., when $det(A)\\ne 0,$ then the image of a two-dimensional object is a two-dimensional object. In particular, the image of a polygon with $n$ vertices is a polygon with $n$ vertices.\n\n- If $T$ is singular, i.e., when $det(A)=0,$ we have two additional subcases:\n\n- If $A$ has at least one nonzero entry, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a one-dimensional line segment.\n\n- If $A$ is the zero matrix, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a point on the plane.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our transformation.\n\nNotice that the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 8-(-4)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a singular nonzero matrix. \n\nTherefore, $T$ is non-invertible, and the image of the quadrilateral under the action of $T$ is a line segment." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407000 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186406997 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407000 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124289" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407000 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407000 #edb/ref 1071 "The affine transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nx=u-v-1,\\,y=3v-2u-6.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ of $T$ is\n\n$$\nu=ax+y+9,\\,v=bx+y+c,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407000 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e92cb69b-a679-593b-8882-9cab8d26a8fb" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407000 #edb/ref 1074 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, writing our transformation in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v-1 \\\\ 3v-2u-6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v \\\\ -2u+3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-2)}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x+1 \\\\ y+6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot (x+1)+1\\cdot (y+6) \\\\ 2\\cdot (x+1)+1\\cdot (y+6)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3x+y+9 \\\\ 2x+y+8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ in coordinate form is\n\n$$\nu=3x+y+9,\\,v=2x+y+8.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=3+2+8=13.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407001 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407005 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407001 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1d9d1d09-adca-5f60-87c8-6eda1712954f" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407001 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186259639 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407002 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "57752ad6-299b-53a6-80c6-38f70d7331f1" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407002 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186406999 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407003 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407002 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407003 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8adcf20b-9143-567f-8916-5a2f8686af25" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407003 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186180095 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407004 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407003 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407004 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b7332e33-ee2f-5908-9f85-c258b5d80b5d" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407004 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407000 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407005 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407004 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407005 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c564b67d-ab6c-5a8c-9962-63cefc9e226d" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186407005 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 